From 62952f2f0922471e75f23ae610203de5622d8d4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:27:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): de-bead stage HARD-GATE exit criteria for
 kernel-native default

The plan/dev/validate/ship/review stage skills mandated Beads shell
scripts as HARD-GATE exit criteria (beads-context.sh set-design/
set-acceptance/stage-transition/validate, dep-guard.sh store-contracts/
check-ripple, "Beads issue created"). On the kernel-native default a
model following them was hard-blocked with no path forward.

- Design/acceptance capture: native Kernel fields via
  `forge update <id> --design` / `--acceptance` (broker-supported).
- Stage transitions + context checks: run the beads-context.sh helper
  only when present ([ -f ... ]); otherwise kernel-native
  `forge comment` / `forge issue show`. Never hard-block on the helper.
- dep-guard contract/ripple review: advisory, guarded on script
  presence, all invocations non-fatal (|| skip). No bd/.beads tokens
  (clears the stage-skills Beads-free gate).
- "Beads issue" wording across the stage surface -> "Forge issue".
- Regenerated the committed .codex/skills mirror (skills-sync drift 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
